{"id":"sax_hamming_distance","title":"SAX Hamming distance","family":"feature-based","definition":"reference","intro_en":"Convert each standardized series to a four-symbol SAX word, then count the fraction of positions with different symbols. This treats every mismatch equally, including adjacent bins; it is a distance between words, with information lost during aggregation and quantization.","intro_zh":"把每条标准化序列转换为四符号 SAX 单词，再统计对应位置符号不同的比例。所有不匹配均等计数，包括相邻区间；它比较符号单词，聚合和量化已经损失信息。","steps_en":["Z-normalize each complete series and use four equal PAA blocks.","Quantize each mean with shared standard-normal quartile breakpoints.","Count mismatching symbols.","Divide the mismatch count by four."],"steps_zh":["对各完整序列做 z 标准化，并计算四个等长 PAA 区间。","使用共享标准正态四分位断点量化各区间均值。","统计符号不匹配数。","将不匹配数除以四。"],"formula":"d = sum_i [SAX_i(x) != SAX_i(y)] / 4","caveats_en":["Gaussian breakpoints are a coding convention; they do not make arbitrary observed signals normally distributed.","Hamming on words does not have the SAX Euclidean lower-bound interpretation.","Both PAA aggregation and quantization can map distinct signals to the same code."],"caveats_zh":["高斯断点是一种编码约定，不会使任意观测信号变成正态分布。","单词上的 Hamming 距离不具有 SAX 欧氏下界的含义。","PAA 聚合和量化都可能把不同信号映射为相同代码。"],"sources":[{"label":"Lin et al. (2007), Experiencing SAX, author copy","url":"https://www.cs.ucr.edu/~stelo/papers/DMKD07b.pdf"},{"label":"Exact illustrative inputs and encoder definitions","url":"https://github.com/ZipengWu365/EchoTime/blob/main/tools/method_animation_data/feature_model_embedding.py"}],"x":[0.0,0.8769216919004693,0.8094744111674236,0.7863961030678929,0.3905255888325767,-0.5769216919004693,-0.6000000000000001,-0.09587051423531628,0.2094744111674235,1.0863961030678926,1.5905255888325764,0.9958705142353173,0.6000000000000002,0.20412948576468337,-0.39052558883257615,0.11360389693210537],"y":[-0.2003300858899106,0.185,0.5703300858899106,1.005,1.0003300858899107,0.3250000000000002,-0.35033008588991066,-0.3550000000000001,0.07966991411008